562
00:21:13,590 --> 00:21:18,080
However, the underlying issue is the study of human cognition

563
00:21:18,080 --> 00:21:20,560
What typically captures a person's attention and focus?

564
00:21:20,560 --> 00:21:22,080
Let's break it down

565
00:21:22,080 --> 00:21:23,080
The book mentions

566
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:26,219
The human brain focuses on things that trigger emotions.

567
00:21:26,219 --> 00:21:29,940
This makes people usually pay attention to others' facial expressions

568
00:21:29,940 --> 00:21:31,460
Including those of small animals

569
00:21:31,460 --> 00:21:34,820
And the brain typically focuses on more unusual thoughts

570
00:21:34,820 --> 00:21:36,620
Or unexpected events

571
00:21:36,620 --> 00:21:38,700
Also, the brain is naturally curious

572
00:21:38,700 --> 00:21:41,400
It wonders what will happen next

573
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:43,480
Another thing is that the brain typically focuses on

574
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:45,060
Things that are threatening

575
00:21:45,060 --> 00:21:49,450
For example, when you're explaining a design pattern to a classmate

576
00:21:49,450 --> 00:21:50,750
Try not to overuse it

577
00:21:50,750 --> 00:21:52,690
When discussing the consequences of overuse

578
00:21:52,690 --> 00:21:55,210
You can send them a scary image

579
00:21:55,210 --> 00:21:58,909
This will make a lasting impression on their brain

580
00:21:58,909 --> 00:22:02,269
The brain also prefers learning by doing

581
00:22:02,269 --> 00:22:04,730
Rather than rote memorization

582
00:22:04,730 --> 00:22:07,730
Because memorization is very energy-consuming

583
00:22:07,730 --> 00:22:09,940
Based on this, we can infer that

584
00:22:09,940 --> 00:22:14,180
We need to make the software documentation as concise as possible

585
00:22:14,180 --> 00:22:16,690
And it's best to have a search function

586
00:22:16,690 --> 00:22:18,130
With a search function

587
00:22:18,130 --> 00:22:21,930
Users can directly ask about what they need

588
00:22:21,930 --> 00:22:23,920
Without having to read through everything

589
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:27,740
So that's how we can save users' attention

